  h1 I. Introduction 
  p When you use Instacuts, you trust us with your personal data. We’re committed to keeping that trust. That starts with helping you understand our privacy practices.  This notice describes the personal data we collect, how it’s used and shared, and your choices regarding this data. We recommend that you read this, which highlights key points about our privacy practices. 
  h5 Last modified: September 1, 2020 
  h5 Effective date: September 1, 2020

  h1 II. Overview 
  h3 Scope 
  p This notice applies to users of Instacuts services anywhere in the world, including users of Instacuts apps, websites, features, or other services. This notice describes how Instacuts and its affiliates collect and use personal data. This notice applies to all users of our apps, websites, features, or other services anywhere in the world, unless covered by a separate privacy notice. This notice specifically applies to 
  p Customers: individuals who request or receive haircut services, including those who receive our services and/or are requested by another individual; 
  p Stylists: individuals who provide, or submit applications to Instacuts to provide, haircuts individually or through partner companies; 
  p Suppliers: individuals or companies that provide equipment, supplies, or other services to Instacuts;
  p Partners: individuals, companies, or organizations who provide, or submit applications to Instacuts to provide, Instacuts services.
  p This notice also governs Instacuts other collections of personal data in connection with services. For example, we may collect the contact information of individuals who use accounts owned by customers or of owners, employees, or representatives of Instacuts partners, or we may collect other personal data in connection with our mapping technology and features.
  p All those subject to this notice are referred to as “users” in this notice. 
  p For users without a Instacuts account: The personal data of users who use Instacuts services arranged by the owners of a Instacuts account is processed in accordance with our contract with the owner of that account, and not as otherwise described in this notice. Such processing may include sharing of user location data with the owner of that account. Please contact the owner of such an account for more information. 
  p Our data practices are subject to applicable laws in the places in which we operate. This means that we engage in the practices described in this notice in a particular state, county, or region only if permitted under the laws of those places. 
  h3 Data controller and transfer 
  p Instacuts is the data controller for the personal data collected in connection with use of Instacuts in the US. Questions, comments, and complaints about Instacuts data practices can be submitted to​ contact@instacuts.us​.   
  h1 III. Data collections and uses 
  h3 Instacuts collects: 
  ul
    li Data provided by users to Instacuts, such as during account creation 
    li Data created during use of our services, such as location, app usage, and device data 
    li Data from other sources, such as partners and third parties that use Instacuts APIs 
    li User profile: We collect data when users create or update their accounts. This may include their name, email, phone number, login name and password, address, profile picture, payment or banking information (including related payment verification information), government identification documents, including driver’s license numbers and images, birthdate, signature, and photo. This also includes vehicle or insurance information of drivers and user settings. We may use the photos submitted by drivers and/or partners to verify their identities, such as through facial recognition technologies. 
    li Background check and identity verification: We collect background check and identity verification information for drivers. This may include information such as driver history or criminal record (where permitted by law), and right to work. This information may be collected by an authorized vendor on Instacuts behalf. 
    li Demographic data: We may collect demographic data about users, including through user surveys. In some countries, we may also receive demographic data about users from third parties. 
    li User content: We collect the information users submit when they contact Instacuts customer support, provide ratings or compliments for other users or partners, or otherwise contact Instacuts. This may include feedback, photographs or other recordings collected by users. 
    li Location data: We collect precise or approximate location data from a user’s mobile device if enabled by the user to do so. For stylists and partners, we collect this data when the app is running in the foreground (app open and on-screen) or background (app open but not on-screen) of their mobile device. Users may use the app without enabling Instacuts to collect location data from their mobile devices. However, this may affect some functionality available in the app.  For example, a user who has not enabled location data collection will have to manually enter their address. In addition, the location data collected during use will be linked to the user’s account, even if they have not enabled location data to be collected from their device, including for purposes of receipt generation, customer support, fraud detection, insurance, and litigation. 
    li Transaction information: We collect transaction information related to the use of our services, including the type of services requested or provided, order details, date and time the service was provided, amount charged, distance traveled, and payment method. Additionally, if someone uses your promotion code, we may associate your name with that person. 
    li Usage data: We collect data about how users interact with our services. This includes data such as access dates and times, app features or pages viewed, app crashes and other system activity, type of browser, and third-party sites or services used before interacting with our services. In some cases, we collect this data through cookies, pixels, tags, and similar tracking technologies that create and maintain unique identifiers. 
    li Device data: We may collect data about the devices used to access our services, including the hardware models, device IP address, operating systems and versions, software, preferred languages, unique device identifiers, advertising identifiers, serial numbers, device motion data, and mobile network data.
    li Communications data: We enable users to communicate with Stylists and Instacuts through our mobile apps and websites. For example, we enable users, Stylists, or to call, text, or send other files to each other (generally without disclosing their telephone numbers to each other). To provide this service, we receive some data regarding the calls, texts, or other communications, including the date and time of the communications and the content of the communications. Instacuts may also use this data for customer support services (including to resolve disputes from users), for safety and security purposes, to improve our products and services, and for analytics. 
    li User feedback, such as ratings, feedback, or compliments. 
    li Users participating in our referral programs. For example, when a user refers another person, we receive the referred person’s personal data from that user. 
    li Account owners who request services for or on behalf of other users, or who enable such users to request or receive services through their accounts. 
    li Users or others providing information in connection with claims or disputes. 
    li Partners through which users create or access their account, such as payment providers, social media services, or apps or websites that use Instacuts APIs or whose APIs Instacuts uses. 
    li Vendors who help us verify users’ identity, background information, and eligibility to work, for regulatory, safety, and security purposes.
    li Insurance, vehicle, or financial services providers for drivers and/or delivery partners.
    li Publicly available sources. 
    li Marketing service providers. 
    p Instacuts may combine the data collected from these sources with other data in its possession. 
    h4 How we use personal data 
    p Instacuts collects and uses data to enable reliable and convenient delivery of our products and services. We also use the data we collect: 
    ul
        li To enhance the safety and security of our users and services 
        li For customer support 
        li For research and development 
        li To enable communications between users 
        li To send marketing and non-marketing communications to users 
        li In connection with legal proceedings 
    p Instacuts does not sell or share user personal data with third parties for their direct marketing, except with users’ consent. 
    p Instacuts uses the data it collects for purposes including: 
    h5 1. ​Providing services and features​. 
    p Instacuts uses the data we collect to provide, personalize, maintain, and improve our products and services.
    p This includes using the data to:  
    ul 
        li Create and update users’ accounts. 
        li Verify drivers’ and partners’ identity, background history, and eligibility to work. 
        li Enable transportation and other services. 
        li Offer, process, or facilitate payments for our services. 
        li Offer, obtain, provide, or facilitate insurance, vehicle, invoicing, or financing solutions in connection with our services. 
        li Track and share the progress of services. 
        li Enable features that allow users to share information with other people, such as when users submit a compliment about a Stylist, refer a friend, or share ETA and location with their contacts. 
        li Enable features to personalize users’ accounts, such as creating bookmarks for favorite places, and to enable quick access to previous services.  
        li Enable Accessibility features that make it easier for users with disabilities to use our services, such as those that enable deaf or hard-of-hearing users to alert Instacuts of their disabilities, allow only text messages from users, and enable receipt of flashing request notifications instead of sound notifications on their mobile device. 
        li Perform internal operations necessary to provide our services, including to troubleshoot software bugs and operational problems; to conduct data analysis, testing, and research; and to monitor and analyze usage and activity trends. 
    h5 2. ​Safety and security​. 
    p We use personal data to help maintain the safety, security, and integrity of our services and users. 
    p This includes: 
    ul 
        li Screening Stylists and partners before enabling their use of our services and at subsequent intervals, including through reviews of background checks, where permitted by law, to help prevent use of our services by unsafe Stylists and/or users. 
        li Using data from Stylists or partners’ devices to help identify unsafe behavior.  
        li Using device, location, profile, usage, and other data to prevent, detect, and combat fraud or unsafe activities. 
        li Using user ratings and feedback as grounds for deactivating Stylists and users with low ratings or who violated any existing or future community guidelines.
    h5 3. ​Customer support​. 
    p Instacuts uses the information we collect (including recordings of customer support calls with notice to and the consent of the user) to provide customer support, including to: 
    ul
        li Direct questions to the appropriate customer support person 
        li Investigate and address user concerns 
        li Monitor and improve our customer support responses and processes 
    h5 4. ​Research and development​. 
    p We may use the data we collect for testing, research, analysis, product development, and machine learning to improve the user experience. This helps us to improve and enhance the safety and security of our services, improve our ability to prevent the use of our services for illegal or improper purposes, develop new features and products, and facilitate insurance and finance solutions in connection with our services. 
    h5 5. ​Marketing​. 
    p Instacuts may use the data we collect to market our services to our users. This includes sending users communications about Instacuts services, features, promotions, sweepstakes, studies, surveys, news, updates, and events. 
    p We may use the data we collect to personalize the marketing communications (including advertisements) that we send, including based on user location, past use of our services, and user preferences and settings. 
    p We may also send users communications regarding elections, ballots, referenda, and other political and notice processes that relate to our services. For example, Instacuts may notify some users by email of ballot measures or pending legislation relating to the availability of our services in those users’ areas. 
    h5 6. ​Non-marketing communications​. 
    p Instacuts may use the data we collect to generate and provide users with receipts; inform them of changes to our terms, services, or policies; or send other communications that aren’t for the purpose of marketing the services or products of Instacuts or our partners. 
    h5 7. ​Legal proceedings and requirements​. 
    p We may use the personal data we collect to investigate or address claims or disputes relating to use of our services, or as otherwise allowed by applicable law, or as requested by regulators, government entities, and official inquiries. 
    h5 8. ​Automated decision-making.​ 
    p We may use personal data to make automated decisions relating to use of our services. This includes: 
    ul 
        li Enabling dynamic pricing, in which the price of a haircut, or other service, is determined based on constantly varying factors such as the estimated time and distance, the predicted route, estimated traffic, and the number of users and Stylists using Instacuts at a given moment. 
        li Matching available Stylists to users requesting services. Users can be matched based on availability, proximity, and other factors.  
        li Determining Stylist ratings, and deactivating Stylists and users with low ratings.  
        li Deactivating users who are identified as having engaged in fraud or activities that may otherwise harm Instacuts, its users, Stylists, and others. In some cases, such as when a user is determined to be abusing our referral program, such behavior may result in automatic deactivation. 
        li Using Stylist location information, and communications between users and Stylists, to identify cancellation fees earned or induced through fraud. For example, if we determine by using such information that a Stylist is delaying a user order to induce a cancellation, we will not charge the user a cancellation fee and will adjust the amounts paid to the Stylist to omit such a fee. 
    h4 Cookies and third-party technologies 
    p Instacuts uses cookies and other identification technologies on our apps, websites, emails, and online ads for purposes described in this notice.  
    p Cookies are small text files that are stored on browsers or devices by websites, apps, online media, and advertisements. Instacuts uses cookies and similar technologies for purposes such as: 
    ul 
        li Authenticating users 
        li Remembering user preferences and settings 
        li Determining the popularity of content 
        li Delivering and measuring the effectiveness of advertising campaigns 
        li Analyzing site traffic and trends, and generally understanding the online behaviors and interests of people who interact with our services 
    p We may also allow others to provide audience measurement and analytics services for us, to serve advertisements on our behalf across the Internet, and to track and report on the performance of those advertisements. These entities may use cookies, web beacons, SDKs, and other technologies to identify the devices used by visitors to our websites, as well as when they visit other online sites and services. 
    h4 Data sharing and disclosure 
    p Some of Instacuts products, services, and features require that we share data with other users or at a user’s request. We may also share data with our affiliates, subsidiaries, and partners, for legal reasons or in connection with claims or disputes. 
    p Instacuts may share the data we collect: 
    p 1. With other users, which includes sharing: 
    ul
        li Users’ first name, rating, and locations with Stylists. 
        li Users’ ratings and feedback, or other information to the extent required by law. 
        li For Stylists, we may share data with users, including name and photo; vehicle make, model, color, license plate, and vehicle photo; location (before and during trip); average rating provided by users; total number of haircuts; length of use of the app; contact information (depending upon applicable laws); and compliments and other feedback submitted by past users. We also provide users with receipts containing information such as a breakdown of amounts charged, Stylist first name, photo, route map, and such other information required on invoices in the region where the Stylist operates. 
        li For those who participate in our referral program, we share certain personal data of referred users, such as number of haircuts provided, with the user who referred them, to the extent relevant to determining the referral bonus. 
    p 2. With the general public 
    p Questions or comments from users submitted through public forums such as blogs and social media pages may be viewable by the public, including any personal data included in the questions or comments submitted by a user. 
    p 3. With the account owner 
    p If a user requests services using an account owned by another party, we may share their order information, including location data, with the owner of that account. 
    p 4. With subsidiaries and affiliates 
    p We may share data with subsidiaries and affiliates to help us provide our services or conduct data processing on our behalf.  
    p 5. With service providers and partners 
    p Instacuts provides data to vendors, consultants, marketing partners, research firms, and other service providers or business partners. These include: 
    ul 
        li Payment processors and facilitators 
        li Background check and identity verification providers  
        li Cloud storage providers 
        li Marketing partners and marketing platform providers, including social media advertising services 
        li Data analytics providers 
        li Research partners, including those performing surveys or research projects  
        li Vendors that assist Instacuts to enhance the safety and security of its apps 
        li Consultants, lawyers, accountants, and other professional service providers 
        li Insurance and financing partners 
    p 6. For legal reasons or in the event of a dispute 
    p Instacuts may share users’ personal data if we believe it’s required by applicable law, regulation, operating license or agreement, legal process or governmental request, or where the disclosure is otherwise appropriate due to safety or similar concerns. This includes sharing personal data with law enforcement officials, public health officials, other government authorities, or other third parties as necessary to enforce our Terms of Service, user agreements, or other policies; to protect our rights or property or the rights, safety, or property of others; or in the event of a claim or dispute relating to the use of our services. If you use another person’s credit card, we may be required by law to share your personal data, including order information, with the owner of that credit card. 
    p This also includes sharing personal data with others in connection with, or during negotiations of, any merger, sale of company assets, consolidation or restructuring, financing, or acquisition of all or a portion of our business by or into another company. 
    p 7. With consent 
    p Instacuts may share a user’s personal data other than as described in this notice if we notify the user and they consent to the sharing. 
    h4 Data retention and deletion 
    p Some of Instacuts products, services, and features require that we share data with other users or at a user’s request. We may also share data with our affiliates, subsidiaries, and partners, for legal reasons or in connection with claims or disputes. 
    p Instacuts may share the data we collect: 
    p 1. With other users, which includes sharing: 
    ul 
        li Users’ first name, rating, and locations with Stylists. 
        li Users’ ratings and feedback, or other information to the extent required by law. 
        li For Stylists, we may share data with users, including name and photo; vehicle make, model, color, license plate, and vehicle photo; location (before and during trip); average rating provided by users; total number of haircuts; length of use of the app; contact information (depending upon applicable laws); and compliments and other feedback submitted by past users. We also provide users with receipts containing information such as a breakdown of amounts charged, Stylist first name, photo, route map, and such other information required on invoices in the region where the Stylist operates. 
        li For those who participate in our referral program, we share certain personal data of referred users, such as number of haircuts provided, with the user who referred them, to the extent relevant to determining the referral bonus. 
