    p Questions or comments from users submitted through public forums such as blogs and social media pages may be viewable by the public, including any personal data included in the questions or comments submitted by a user. 
    p 3. With the account owner 
    p If a user requests services using an account owned by another party, we may share their order information, including location data, with the owner of that account. 
    p 4. With subsidiaries and affiliates 
    p We may share data with subsidiaries and affiliates to help us provide our services or conduct data processing on our behalf.  
    p 5. With service providers and partners 
    p Instacuts provides data to vendors, consultants, marketing partners, research firms, and other service providers or business partners. These include: 
    ul 
        li Payment processors and facilitators 
        li Background check and identity verification providers  
        li Cloud storage providers 
        li Marketing partners and marketing platform providers, including social media advertising services 
        li Data analytics providers 
        li Research partners, including those performing surveys or research projects  
        li Vendors that assist Instacuts to enhance the safety and security of its apps 
        li Consultants, lawyers, accountants, and other professional service providers 
        li Insurance and financing partners 
    p 6. For legal reasons or in the event of a dispute 
    p Instacuts may share users’ personal data if we believe it’s required by applicable law, regulation, operating license or agreement, legal process or governmental request, or where the disclosure is otherwise appropriate due to safety or similar concerns. This includes sharing personal data with law enforcement officials, public health officials, other government authorities, or other third parties as necessary to enforce our Terms of Service, user agreements, or other policies; to protect our rights or property or the rights, safety, or property of others; or in the event of a claim or dispute relating to the use of our services. If you use another person’s credit card, we may be required by law to share your personal data, including order information, with the owner of that credit card.
